cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these artefacts, please cite the archived Zenodo record rather than the repository URL."
title: "unit-gap-artefacts: machine-checkable artefacts for a refutation of Theorem 2 of arXiv:2603.08033"
abstract: >-
  DRAT proof certificates, exhaustive NPN-class gap censuses, exact-synthesis
  encoders, and a Lean 4 formalization supporting a refutation of Theorem 2 of
  Krinkin, "The Unit Gap: How Sharing Works in Boolean Circuits"
  (arXiv:2603.08033). The counterexample is parity on three inputs, where the
  DAG optimum is 6 gates and the formula optimum is 9, so the gap is 3 rather
  than the claimed maximum of 1. The refutation itself is classical: Schnorr
  (1976) gives the circuit side and Khrapchenko's bound the formula side, which
  together already force a gap of at least 2. The exact value 3 is certified
  here.
authors:
